---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import SchemaMarkup from '../components/SchemaMarkup.astro';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const schema = [
  webPageSchema('Accessibility Statement', 'eLan Technology accessibility statement - our accessibility-first approach, feedback channel and current limitations.', '/accessibility-statement/'),
  breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Accessibility Statement', url: '/accessibility-statement/' }]),
];
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  description="eLan Technology accessibility statement - our accessibility-first approach, feedback channel and current limitations."
  lastUpdated="2026-09-24"
>
  <SchemaMarkup schema={schema} />

  <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
  <p>
    eLan Technology is committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities. We
    believe that everyone deserves equal access to information and services online, regardless of
    ability. We use an accessibility-first development approach for this website and continue to
    review barriers as content, code and third-party services change. Client-project requirements
    and testing are separately defined in each accepted scope.
  </p>

  <h2>Conformance Status</h2>
  <p>
    Our present target for this website is WCAG 2.1 Level AA. This is a conformance target, not a
    certification or a claim that every page, third-party component or future content change is free
    from accessibility barriers.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> - Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.1 published by the
      World Wide Web Consortium (W3C), used as the primary technical reference for review and remediation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act)</strong> - legal applicability and compliance are
      fact-specific. WCAG-informed work can support accessibility but does not by itself constitute a
      legal certification.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act</strong> - relevant requirements may apply to
      particular United States federal contexts; they are not automatically applicable to every website.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Technical Specifications</h2>
  <p>
    Our website relies on the following technologies to deliver content and support accessible use:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>HTML5</li>
    <li>CSS3 / Tailwind CSS v4</li>
    <li>JavaScript (Astro Islands architecture - minimal and purposeful)</li>
    <li>WAI-ARIA (Web Accessibility Initiative - Accessible Rich Internet Applications)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Measures Taken</h2>
  <p>
    eLan Technology has implemented the following specific accessibility measures on this website:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Semantic HTML5 landmarks:</strong> we use <code>&lt;header&gt;</code>,
      <code>&lt;main&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code>, and other
      landmark elements to define page regions clearly for screen reader users.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Skip navigation link:</strong> shared page templates place a "Skip to main content"
      link before the primary navigation so keyboard users can bypass repeated controls.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Image alternatives:</strong> meaningful images are intended to include useful text
      alternatives, while decorative images should be hidden from assistive technology. New and
      changed content requires continued editorial review.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Colour contrast:</strong> the design system targets WCAG 2.1 AA contrast thresholds;
      individual images, embedded content and future changes may require separate verification.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Keyboard use:</strong> navigation, forms and custom controls are designed for keyboard
      operation and are reviewed when interaction patterns change.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Visible focus indicators:</strong> the interface provides a visible focus treatment for
      keyboard interaction; third-party components may use their own focus presentation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Labelled form fields:</strong> first-party forms are designed with programmatically
      associated labels and should not rely on placeholder text alone.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Error communication:</strong> first-party validation is designed to identify the
      affected field and describe the correction needed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Responsive and zoomable:</strong> layouts are designed to reflow and remain usable at
      increased zoom. Complex tables, code, third-party content and unusually long strings may need
      horizontal scrolling or an alternative presentation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Flashing content:</strong> we do not intentionally publish content that flashes at a
      frequency known to create a seizure risk.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Reduced motion support:</strong> we respect the <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>
      CSS media query. Animations and transitions are disabled or minimised for users who have
      indicated a preference for reduced motion.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Logical reading order:</strong> the visual reading order of content matches the
      underlying DOM order, ensuring screen readers present content in a logical sequence without
      relying on CSS positioning.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Page language declared:</strong> shared templates declare English as the primary page
      language to support pronunciation and language processing by assistive technology.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Descriptive link text:</strong> we aim to use meaningful, context-aware link text and
      avoid ambiguous standalone phrases when creating or revising content.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known Limitations</h2>
  <p>
    We are committed to continuous improvement. The following known limitations are being addressed:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Legacy PDF documents:</strong> some older PDF files on this website may not be fully
      accessible to screen reader users. If you require an accessible version of any document, please
      contact us and we will provide an alternative format.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Third-party embeds:</strong> embedded tools such as Calendly (scheduling) and Google
      Maps are provided by third parties and are beyond our direct control. We encourage users
      requiring accessible alternatives to contact us directly.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Feedback and Contact</h2>
  <p>
    We actively welcome feedback on the accessibility of our website. If you encounter any barriers,
    have difficulty accessing content, or would like to report an accessibility issue, please get in
    touch:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Email: <a href="mailto:accessibility@elan-tech.net">accessibility@elan-tech.net</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/918788834630">+91 8788834630</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Phone: <a href="tel:+919822231642">+91 9822231642</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      Address: <a href="https://share.google/PklD3tFGBBqsPHjli" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eLan Technology, Basement Floor, PTG IT Park, Plot No. 21, IT Park Rd, Gayatri Nagar, Nagpur, Maharashtra 440022, India</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We aim to acknowledge accessibility enquiries within <strong>2 business days</strong>.
    Investigation and remediation time depends on the barrier, affected content and third-party involvement.
  </p>

  <h2>Formal Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you have raised an accessibility concern with us and are not satisfied with the response or
    the resolution timeline, you are entitled to contact the relevant regulatory authority or
    disability rights body in your jurisdiction.
  </p>

  <h2>Assessment Approach</h2>
  <p>
    eLan Technology self-assesses the accessibility of this website using the following tools and
    methods:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Automated checks</strong> - suitable scanning tools can identify a subset of detectable
      issues; automated scores are not treated as proof of conformance.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Lighthouse reviews</strong> - used as one development signal on selected templates and
      important user journeys.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Manual keyboard review</strong> - selected templates and important interactions are
      reviewed for focus order, visibility and operability, with repeat checks after material changes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Assistive-technology review</strong> - representative journeys may be reviewed with
      technologies such as NVDA and VoiceOver. This is not continuous coverage of every combination.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Statement Date</h2>
  <p>
    This Accessibility Statement was last reviewed and updated on <strong>24 September 2026</strong>.
    We review this statement at least annually and whenever significant changes are made to the
    website.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
